    "q-115166": {
      "dom_id": "step-q115166",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/b732a88bc43e0073d7056c536469ac0b959988dd45f385a605ff57432827f334.png)\n\nThe graph above is a translation of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$ Identify the equation that generated the graph.",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the left by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/b6f0f056c74b60cc8a548ae14d10512c929f378285591996d440da97cb3ed19e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x+3}-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
